 - [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
 - [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
-- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When a submission names a base revision that is not the visit's current head revision, the system SHALL retain it as a competing revision without changing the visit's head.
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return its current payload, head revision ID, unresolved-work flag, and — when the flag is set — the list of open competing revisions.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a visit's first submission is accepted, the system SHALL store it as the visit's first revision with no base revision.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission names the visit's current head revision as its base, the system SHALL append it as the new head revision.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: While a visit has unresolved competing revisions, the system SHALL keep the visit's current state at the last agreed head revision except when a recorded resolution moves it.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a coordinator resolution adopts one of a visit's competing revisions, the system SHALL set the visit's current state to that revision's payload, clear the unresolved-work flag, and retain every competing revision.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a submission names a base revision that does not exist or belongs to a different visit, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a caller retrieves a visit's revision history, the system SHALL return every retained revision of that visit with its base revision reference, author, and receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a submission arrives with an invalid field value or a plot reference that is not in the site catalog, the system SHALL reject it without storing any revision.
